WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.012 --> 00:00:02.762
(relaxing music)

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.430
- [Johnny] I'm looking
at a reservoir right now

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:11.060
that is full of water
from a different country.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:12.810
- [Male Speaker] For a
country that is surrounded

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.140
by water, you might not expect Cyprus

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.940
to be suffering a shortage.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.166
The answer, pump it in;
the question, where from?

00:00:21.166 --> 00:00:23.930
(soothing electronic music)

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:27.650
- But the reality is this
water is not just water.

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.490
It represents something so much bigger.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:33.334
This entire project is happening
for a very specific reason.

00:00:33.334 --> 00:00:35.050
(funky music)

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.420
The flags on the side
of this dam represent

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.985
this joint venture between Turkey,

00:00:39.985 --> 00:00:44.460
and the so-called Turkish
Republic of Northern Cyprus.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.330
A country that doesn't technically exist,

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.850
but Turkey wants it to exist.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:52.580
And that's why they
built this umbilical cord

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:55.270
from their country, to the country

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:57.909
they're trying to make a real country.

00:00:57.909 --> 00:01:00.700
(funky music)

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.680
I want to talk to the
people who live here,

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.170
to understand what it feels like

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:07.543
to live in a country that doesn't exist.

00:01:07.543 --> 00:01:08.390
(energetic electronic music)

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:09.750
- [Male Speaker] Tanks of the Turkish Army

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:12.017
are about to compete
their victory in Cyprus.

00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:15.580
The Turkish army has conquered
that part of the island,

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.870
which she thinks should
belong to the Turks.

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:19.720
- [Male Speaker 2] There are
no trade and customs barriers

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.780
between North and South, neither side

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.040
recognizes the other's ports of entry.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.470
- [Male Speaker] Turkey could
draw the Southern boundary

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:30.503
of what would virtually be a
new state of Turkish Cyprus.

