00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.703
And now let's get back
to the island of Cyprus.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.060
- [Johnny] My hope is that this pipeline

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.830
will make a lot more
sense in like 10 minutes.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:33.100
By then, you will understand
what this really means,

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.830
both geopolitically, and on a human level.

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:38.260
It'll also make sense how
this pipeline is connected

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:40.160
to the people who live here.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:43.160
Like this guy, Vedat, a Turkish Cypriot

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.200
who sometimes wishes he
could get off this island.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:50.484
- I'm not hugely ambitious,
but I do want to leave-

00:03:50.484 --> 00:03:52.610
- Yeah.
- if I can.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:54.390
- [Johnny] But for all
of that to make sense,

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:57.650
you have to understand the
Turkish side of the story

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:00.151
of what happened in 1974.

00:04:00.151 --> 00:04:03.068
(slow piano music)

00:04:06.238 --> 00:04:10.071
- (speaking foreign language)

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:22.520
- [Johnny] The Cypriots became independent

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.520
from the British in 1960.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:27.730
Soon, the two groups on
the island were clashing.

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:31.270
The Greek Cypriot majority
bullying and massacring

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:34.280
the Turkish Cypriot
minority, who were driven out

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:36.970
of their villages into
camps around the country.

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:39.910
This was one reason why, in 1974,

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:42.410
Turkey felt emboldened to intervene,

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:45.440
to save the Turkish Cypriots
from this persecution.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:47.780
- [Male Speaker] It's no
wonder that the Turks rejoice,

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:51.105
no wonder that the siege is
but a bad memory from a past,

00:04:51.105 --> 00:04:52.523
which will never return.

00:04:53.678 --> 00:04:57.511
- (speaking foreign language)

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:00.870
- [Johnny] Turkey took over
the North of this island,

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:03.940
forcing Greek Cypriots to
leave their homes empty,

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:06.060
only to be filled by Turkish Cypriots

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:07.683
coming north for protection.

00:05:09.178 --> 00:05:10.420
(overlapping background voices)

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:11.760
- [Male Speaker] They won't return

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.214
while the Turks are there.

00:05:13.214 --> 00:05:16.214
(tense piano music)

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:19.930
- My new mechanic friend, Dogay,

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:22.750
came to this village that
used to be a Greek village,

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:25.770
but was now empty from
everyone having fled.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:26.603
And he found a home.

00:05:26.603 --> 00:05:29.965
So this is- just moved in here.

00:05:29.965 --> 00:05:30.798
- [Male Speaker 3] They moved in.

00:05:30.798 --> 00:05:32.580
- [Johnny] And the
Turkish military gave him,

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.690
and his family, a home to live in.

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:36.690
Oh, this is the house
that they moved into.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:37.523
- [Male Speaker 3] Yes.

00:05:37.523 --> 00:05:38.740
- When they arrived to this house,

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:43.030
they found all the mundane
things of a normal life:

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:45.932
homework from a high
school geometry class.

00:05:45.932 --> 00:05:46.765
- [Male Speaker 3] This is schoolwork.

00:05:46.765 --> 00:05:47.697
- [Johnny] Schoolwork?

00:05:47.697 --> 00:05:52.697
Furniture and art, lots
of art, original art.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:55.633
The people living here
must've been artists.

00:05:55.633 --> 00:05:59.500
- (speaking foreign language)

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:02.410
- [Johnny] How did it
feel to arrive to a house

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:05.621
that had people's art
and belongings in it?

00:06:05.621 --> 00:06:08.176
- (speaking foreign language)

00:06:08.176 --> 00:06:09.740
(energetic electronic music)

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:12.430
- [Johnny] By August,
1974, Turkey had taken

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:15.070
all of this land, which was now considered

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:17.260
a safe haven for Turkish Cypriots.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.620
But the world didn't like this,

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:21.320
they were calling this
an illegal occupation.

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:25.140
So Turkey held fast to their
line of being protectors.

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:27.190
- [Male Speaker] Generals
of the Turkish high command,

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:30.310
their victory complete, arrived
in triumph to acknowledge

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:32.568
the greetings of those they'd saved.

00:06:32.568 --> 00:06:37.349
(energetic electronic music with piano)

00:06:37.349 --> 00:06:41.182
- (speaking foreign language)

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:46.870
- [Male Speaker 3] But then
freedoms are never given.

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:48.490
You have to take 'em.

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:49.940
I'm afraid we had to do that,

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:52.270
only Turkey could've helped us.

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:54.740
- [Johnny] Turkish Cypriots
felt saved by Turkey,

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:57.640
but Turkey's motives for
taking over all of this land

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:01.602
wasn't just about saving
100,000 or so Turkish Cypriots.

00:07:01.602 --> 00:07:03.410
(tense electronic music)

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:07.560
Starting in 1974, Turkey set
about on a decades-long project

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:10.220
of turning this land
that they just took over,

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:13.690
into a country-like space,
that could help fulfill

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:16.040
Turkey's bigger objectives in the region.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:19.530
While also ensuring that
this 35% of the island

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:22.480
would never be reunited
with the rest of the island.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:26.230
(energetic electronic music)

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:29.660
There's this phrase we use
in international relations,

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:31.370
called, "Facts on the ground".

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:35.160
It describes what geopolitical
situations actually look like

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.370
on the ground, versus
what they technically

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:40.550
should look like, according
to laws and treaties.

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:42.820
So while all this land in Northern Cyprus,

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:45.960
technically on paper,
belongs to the EU country

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:48.820
called the Republic of Cyprus, in reality,

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:51.160
the facts on the ground say otherwise.

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:53.270
The facts that we're
talking about, in this case,

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:55.890
are usually humans, real people

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:59.300
occupying space and building
physical infrastructure.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.520
It's the same reason why
Israel subsidizes people

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:03.600
to live out here in the West Bank,

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:06.770
to make it harder to ever
create a Palestinian State.

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:08.870
Or why Russia sends hundreds of people

00:08:08.870 --> 00:08:12.980
to this remote island, to work
a coal mine that loses money,

00:08:12.980 --> 00:08:15.830
but that helps them establish
a physical presence here,

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:18.040
in case oil is ever
discovered in the Arctic.

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:20.480
The upshot is that no matter
what it says on paper,

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:22.680
it's really hard to say that a space

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:24.110
isn't a part of a country,

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:27.130
when it looks and acts like
a part of that country.

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:28.260
So this is the approach

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:31.350
that Turkey decided to take after 1974.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:33.650
The Turkish government put
out radio advertisements

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:36.480
to rural parts of Turkey,
telling low-wage workers

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:39.690
that they could resettle on a
nearby Mediterranean island,

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:43.840
where they would be given a
home, a farm, animals, money.

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:46.530
More than 30,000 Turkish
Nationals took them up

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:49.340
on the offer, and headed
for the occupied island.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.620
They filled these empty Greek homes.

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:53.750
They started a new life.

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:55.570
- [Interviewer] What do
you pay for the house?

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:59.250
- For the time, we don't
pay. Hasn't come up yet.

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:00.570
- [Interviewer] It's the
property of the government

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:01.403
now, is it?

00:09:01.403 --> 00:09:02.236
- Yes, it is, yes.

00:09:03.129 --> 00:09:04.240
- [Interviewer] Are you worried, at all,

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:06.130
that the original owner might somehow

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:07.980
have some opportunity to get it back?

00:09:08.859 --> 00:09:12.615
- I don't think so, no, (indistinct).

00:09:12.615 --> 00:09:14.020
- [Interviewer] You just don't
think it'll happen, you mean?

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:15.310
- No, I don't think so, no.

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:16.440
- [Johnny] But here's the thing.

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:19.990
Turkish Cypriots are not the
same as Turkish Nationals.

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:22.910
While they both have cultural
roots in the Ottoman Empire,

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.930
many of these Turkish
settlers align politically,

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:28.760
culturally, and religiously
with mainland Turkey,

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:30.350
more than with Cyprus.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:33.900
- Many Turkish Cypriots
feel that their lifestyle,

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:38.890
and their culture, are being threatened

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:41.260
by the current Turkish government.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:45.440
By building Mosques,
by trying to take part

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:47.780
in the change in the culture.

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:51.200
Generally speaking, Turkey
Cypriots are very secular,

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:54.330
part of an island, easygoing lifestyle,

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:55.870
maybe even less religious,

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:59.001
or enjoy their beliefs in privacy.

00:09:59.001 --> 00:10:02.834
- (speaking foreign language)

00:10:05.529 --> 00:10:09.362
- (speaking foreign language)

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:11.770
- [Johnny] In the decades that followed,

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:14.122
Turkish mainlanders kept coming.

00:10:14.122 --> 00:10:17.955
- (speaking foreign language)

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:27.630
- [Johnny] Over the years,
Turkey helped the Cypriots

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:28.990
establish a new government.

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:31.930
They renamed all of the
villages from Greek names,

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:33.910
to Turkish names, and eventually,

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:35.960
they declared this place a new country,

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:39.630
the Turkish Republic of
Northern Cyprus, or TRNC.

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:41.890
The rest of the world,
of course, rejected this.

00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:44.000
This was not a new country, it was still

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:46.810
the Republic of Cyprus,
with just 35% of it

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:48.300
being occupied by Turkey.

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:51.020
And indeed, efforts from
the international community

00:10:51.020 --> 00:10:53.310
focused on reunifying this island,

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:55.030
making it one Cyprus.

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:57.270
Turkey knew that the
only way to stop this,

00:10:57.270 --> 00:11:00.770
was not just to send
people to occupy the land,

00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:02.370
but also to make this place

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.840
feel and look like a real country,

00:11:04.840 --> 00:11:09.030
one that is deeply reliant on
Turkey; facts on the ground.

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:11.130
So I'm now at a base for the Coast Guard,

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:12.670
about to get on a boat.

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:14.740
Wow, okay.

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:15.770
Good morning, hi there.

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:16.867
- [Male Speaker 4] Good morning, sir.

00:11:16.867 --> 00:11:18.075
- [Johnny] How are you?

00:11:18.075 --> 00:11:21.010
(tense electronic music)

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:23.490
I rode with the TRNC Coast Guard.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:25.780
It was kind of a bizarre experience.

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:28.300
Halfway through the ride,
the leader of the boat,

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:30.540
who was sort of escorting us on this trip,

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:33.730
started prompting me to
get shots of this flag,

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:37.520
the TRNC flag, which looks
very similar to Turkey's flag.

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:40.050
He asked me a few times to get this shot.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:43.010
For all of the military
and government ridealongs

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:45.740
I've been on, this was a strange moment.

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:48.730
And it clearly revealed
why the TRNC Coast Guard

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:50.870
let me come here in the first place,

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:53.140
why it was fairly easy to get access.

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:56.877
Turkey wants the world to see
that this is a real country.

00:11:56.877 --> 00:12:00.230
"Look, it has a real
military with a real flag."

00:12:00.230 --> 00:12:03.090
But in reality, if you
peek under the surface,

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:05.560
you'll see that this TRNC
military has anywhere

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:08.460
from 3-9,000 troops on the island;

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:11.110
compare that with the
more than 30,000 troops

00:12:11.110 --> 00:12:12.430
that Turkey has here.

00:12:12.430 --> 00:12:15.800
And, in fact, two thirds
of the entire TRNC budget

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:17.090
is funded by Turkey.

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:20.458
The TRNC is a place sponsored by Turkey.

00:12:20.458 --> 00:12:23.420
(tense electronic music)

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:26.380
And they eagerly let me
come cover their military,

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:28.570
or get shots of their border crossing,

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:31.470
so that I would broadcast
these "facts on the ground"

00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:35.100
to the world, to show how
country-like this place feels.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:36.863
And indeed, admittedly, it does.

00:12:37.754 --> 00:12:40.587
(energetic music)

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:47.297
So the big question I have is, "Why?"

00:12:47.297 --> 00:12:48.500
Why does Turkey do this thing

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.300
that the rest of the world condemns,

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:52.930
just so that they can
have 35% of this island?

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:56.220
The first answer to that is
just general geopolitics,

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:59.110
whose tagline is, "Control more land."

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:00.910
Especially land that recently

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:03.690
had a deposit of oil
and gas off its shores.

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:05.910
- [Male Speaker 4] The
Greek-dominated Republic of Cyprus

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:08.450
is now set to profit from natural gas.

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:09.940
- So on the agenda, in Brussels,

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:10.773
yesterday, was-

00:13:10.773 --> 00:13:11.606
- (multiple voices) Turkey.

00:13:11.606 --> 00:13:13.580
- Turkey's drilling for oil and gas.

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:15.920
- In the hotly-contested
East Mediterranean.

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:17.270
- Off the coast of Cyprus.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:18.410
- [Male Speaker 4] People here are worried

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:19.540
about another war.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:20.740
- [Male Speaker] A single incident

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:23.800
could easily draw the region
into a devastating war.

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:25.330
- [Johnny] Turkey claims that all of this

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:28.214
is the economic water of the TRNC,

00:13:28.214 --> 00:13:30.840
but no one on Earth would let that happen.

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:34.700
So in response, Turkey opened
a new base on the TRNC,

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:37.410
with drones and other
military infrastructure,

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:40.113
just to reinforce their
claim with firepower.

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:42.540
The other major reason for all of this

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:44.710
is just straight-up nationalism.

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.857
The current president
in Turkey is sort of a,

00:13:46.857 --> 00:13:49.560
"Make Turkey great again," kind of guy.

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:51.460
Owning Cyprus is just another place

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:54.770
for him to spread that
ideology and religious fervor.

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:58.480
And PS, that Turkish Nationalism,
is also spread vigorously

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:01.670
by his army of Turkish
Nationalists on the internet.

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:04.260
You'll definitely see them in
the comments of this video.

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:06.810
But yeah, Turkey wants to
keep this part of Cyprus.

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:08.600
They don't want it to
fall back into the hands

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:10.730
of the Republic of Cyprus,
where it would become

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:13.070
a member of the EU, and part of a country

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:14.960
that isn't super friendly to Turkey.

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:17.790
Okay, so geopolitics, blah-blah-blah.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:19.150
What about the people?

00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:21.670
The people who are actually
living here every day.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:23.430
We can look on a map all day long,

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:26.960
but I came here to talk to
the people who live in a place

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:29.411
that is more and more reliant on Turkey.

00:14:29.411 --> 00:14:33.161
(energetic electronic music)

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:40.050
(soft electronic music)

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:42.650
How do you feel about
Turkey, the country, today,

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:43.960
and its presence here?

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:45.440
Does it feel protective?

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:47.350
- To be honest, to me, it
doesn't feel protective.

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:52.350
It feels rather like
digesting conquered territory.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:56.390
That might sound extreme to
some, but that's how I see it.

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:59.970
- You live in a country
that the rest of the world

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:01.510
doesn't recognize as a country.

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:02.590
- Yes.

00:15:02.590 --> 00:15:04.740
- How does that feel to you?

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:06.720
- It feels secluded, to be honest.

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:09.567
- [Johnny] This pseudo-country
of Northern Cyprus

00:15:09.567 --> 00:15:12.810
isn't able to trade
with any other country,

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:14.110
any goods that come in here,

00:15:14.110 --> 00:15:15.830
have to go through Turkey first.

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:18.750
Any goods that go out of
here, have to go to Turkey,

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:21.010
and be handled or modified in some way,

00:15:21.010 --> 00:15:24.060
so that they are technically
Turkish, all of a sudden,

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:26.000
and then they can be
shipped out into the world.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:28.040
- [Male Speaker] Only 63
foreign ships were handled

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:31.310
at Famagusta last year, for the
regime is not yet recognized

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:32.610
by anyone but Turkey.

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:35.030
The biggest single user
of Famagusta's port

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:38.430
is the Turkish military;
137 ships last year.

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:42.270
- I have to say this, like
everything in the TRNC's

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:46.020
like a cheap knockoff of
the original. (chuckles)

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:48.450
- And then you have the airport
here in Northern Cyprus.

00:15:48.450 --> 00:15:50.840
Again, it's sort of an illegal airport,

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:54.580
it only flies to Turkey, it
can't fly to any other country.

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:56.870
- It feels like there's the TRNC,

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:57.837
and then there's the world.

00:15:57.837 --> 00:15:58.670
- Yeah.

00:15:58.670 --> 00:15:59.860
- So everything else is different here.

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:00.693
- Yeah.

00:16:00.693 --> 00:16:03.880
- Most of the diplomas
that you get from TRNC,

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:06.900
they aren't recognized
anywhere in the world.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.020
I think there are exceptions, to like,

00:16:09.020 --> 00:16:11.250
one or two universities, but most of them

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:14.370
are practically useless if you're planning

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:18.010
to go abroad, because
they're not recognized.

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:19.650
- [Johnny] All of this
makes the people here

00:16:19.650 --> 00:16:21.590
locked into Turkey's world,

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:24.810
for trade, for business, for security,

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:27.930
for government funding, it's all Turkey.

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:29.430
- [Male Speaker]
Everywhere, mainland Turkey

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:31.240
casts a giant shadow.

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:33.710
What then of the Turkish Cypriot identity?

00:16:33.710 --> 00:16:35.580
Cyprus is already divided.

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:38.795
Will the North soon become
just another Turkish province?

00:16:38.795 --> 00:16:42.365
(slow electronic music)

00:16:42.365 --> 00:16:46.198
- (speaking foreign language)

00:16:52.600 --> 00:16:54.830
- Well, ultimately, I believe that Cyprus

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:57.080
belongs to Cypriots, Greek Cypriots

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:58.360
and Turkish Cypriots alike,

00:16:58.360 --> 00:16:59.826
but they should have the final say

00:16:59.826 --> 00:17:01.890
in the future of their country.

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:03.870
- [Johnny] And that gets
us back to this pipeline.

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:07.560
The one that sends water from
Southern Turkey into Cyprus

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:09.940
to provide drinking water
for the people here.

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:11.980
Is it starting to make more sense now?

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:15.060
I called this "an umbilical
cord", because it represents

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:17.770
just one of the many ways that Turkey,

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:20.030
who calls themselves the mother country,

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:22.560
has made the TRNC reliant on them.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:25.020
Now, listen, it's one thing
to fund the government

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:27.400
and the military, and be the only gateway

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:28.740
to the global economy.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:31.880
But this is water, for
heaven's sake; it's survival.

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:34.410
This is a much deeper level of reliance.

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:37.570
This reliance was made very clear in 2020,

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:39.190
when the pipeline burst.

00:17:39.190 --> 00:17:41.190
The towns that have their water systems

00:17:41.190 --> 00:17:42.970
now linked into this pipeline

00:17:42.970 --> 00:17:46.020
were without water for
days, sometimes weeks.

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:49.010
They eventually fixed the
pipeline, but all of this revealed

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:51.410
just how reliant these people now are,

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:53.700
on the country across the sea.

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:56.170
Turkish Cypriots, of course,
would never go for this

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:57.700
if they had another option.

00:17:57.700 --> 00:18:00.850
But the reality is, they don't,
because they needed water.

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:02.550
So they took the gift.

00:18:02.550 --> 00:18:06.060
- They'll say, "We came and
we saved you, you need us."

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:09.650
So all of this- sort of
like, yes, they did help

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:14.010
when we needed it, back in the day.

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:18.770
But just feels like now
we're being held hostage

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:20.690
by the fact that they helped.

00:18:20.690 --> 00:18:22.430
- [Johnny] All of these
reliances on Turkey,

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:24.700
make it less and less
likely that this island

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:26.780
will ever find unity again.

00:18:26.780 --> 00:18:29.120
With every Turkish
National that moves here,

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:32.130
or every bit of money
used to build the military

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:34.790
or government here, with
every infrastructure project,

00:18:34.790 --> 00:18:38.530
real peace on this island
becomes less and less possible.

00:18:38.530 --> 00:18:41.870
Facts on the ground,
more and more every year,

00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:43.500
just as Turkey intended.

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:45.560
But listen, I want to
make one thing clear.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.930
This isn't as simple as Turkey

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:50.360
holding the people of Cyprus hostage,

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:52.070
it's more nuanced than that.

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:54.220
Especially if you were a Turkish Cypriot

00:18:54.220 --> 00:18:56.631
in the '60s and '70s.

00:18:56.631 --> 00:19:00.548
- (speaking foreign language)

00:19:01.498 --> 00:19:05.331
- (speaking foreign language)

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:11.880
- [Johnny] These were
minorities who were bullied

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:14.200
and massacred, and they found refuge

00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:16.080
when Turkey came in to save them.

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:18.780
That's a reality that's
not easy to forget.

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:21.170
But in the end, it's
clear that even despite

00:19:21.170 --> 00:19:24.480
the pro-Turkey feelings
among some Turkish Cypriots,

00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:26.060
what Turkey has done to this island

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:28.740
is prioritized Turkey's interests,

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:30.590
and not the interests of the people.

00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:33.330
Who, even though they
received all of these gifts,

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:36.590
really pay the price of being
Turkey's political pond.

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:38.940
Something that has been
a theme for the people

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:42.123
on this island for literally
thousands of years.

00:19:43.261 --> 00:19:46.594
(slow electronic music)

